invariant: INV-53
file: proof/coverage.py
catches: test/lint-matrix.sh
reason: the reach merge skips a part that did not report, so the merged
  table loses that part's harnesses and the merge job stays green. Only
  the nightly's merge-reach-table job ran the merge before. Now
  lint-matrix writes the parts with each one absent in turn. It requires
  a failed merge and a row for each harness of the absent part.

--- old
        part = parts[k][2] if k in parts else None
--- new
        if k not in parts:
            continue
        part = parts[k][2]
